! C3MechLiteV4.0.1 and C3MechCoreV4.0.1 have been generated based on C3MechV4.0.1 formulated         !
! by the Computational Chemistry Consortium (C3), a collaborative research organization              !
! including the University of Galway, Politecnico di Milano, RWTH Aachen University,                 !
! Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory, Argonne National Laboratory and Convergent Science.        !
!                                                                                                    !
! < C3MechLiteV4.0.1 >                                                                               !
! - 61 species and 519 reactions                                                                     !
! - Intended to simulate natural gas combustion with NOx chemistry                                   !
! - Targeting H2, CO, NH3, CH4, CH3OH, Natural gas (CH4 + C2H6/C3H8), and NOx                        !
!                                                                                                    !
! < C3MechCoreV4.0.1 >                                                                               !
! - 118 species and 1006 reactions                                                                   !
! - Covering a wider range of fuels up to C3                                                         !
! - Targeting H2, CO, NH3, CH4, CH3OH, C2H6, DME, C2H5OH, C3H8, and NOx                              !
!                                                                                                    !
! Reaction counts listed above refer to the Cantera-compatible mechanism files (reference values).   !
! CHEMKIN-Pro files show different reaction counts because LOWMX/TROEMX and                          !
! LOWSP/TROESP keywords encode species-specific falloff behavior within grouped reactions.           !
